WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:06.760
Okay, so now we can understand exactly what is an SQL query.

00:06.800 --> 00:11.040
Now normally your data is inside the table and your table is inside the database.

00:11.040 --> 00:15.120
And now you might have a question from the business like what is the total sales.

00:15.120 --> 00:17.160
What is the total number of customers.

00:17.160 --> 00:22.000
So any question that you have in your mind and you want to go and ask your data, you want to go and

00:22.000 --> 00:24.400
retrieve data from the database.

00:24.400 --> 00:29.480
And in order to do that you have to talk to the database using its language, the SQL.

00:29.520 --> 00:34.560
So in order to do that, you're going to go and write a query where you write inside the query something

00:34.560 --> 00:36.360
called select statements.

00:36.360 --> 00:39.200
And with that you are asking the database for data.

00:39.200 --> 00:43.200
So once you execute your query the database is going to go and fetch your data.

00:43.200 --> 00:46.280
And then it prepares the results to be sent back to you.

00:46.280 --> 00:50.600
So with that you are asking the database question by writing a query.

00:50.600 --> 00:55.560
And the database is going to process your query and answer your question by sending back data.

00:55.560 --> 00:59.000
And with that, we are like reading our data from the database.

00:59.000 --> 01:04.840
And the queries will not modify anything, will not change the data inside your tables, or even change

01:04.840 --> 01:06.480
the structure of the database.

01:06.480 --> 01:11.160
So you use select statement only in order to read something from the database.

01:11.160 --> 01:14.160
You just want to retrieve data from the database.

01:14.160 --> 01:16.240
So this is what we mean with a query.

01:20.120 --> 01:25.160
And now my friends each SQL query has usually different sections different components.

01:25.160 --> 01:26.400
We call them clauses.

01:26.400 --> 01:32.040
And this is amazing because you can have enough tools to write a query that matches any question that

01:32.040 --> 01:33.160
you have about your data.

01:33.160 --> 01:38.040
So what we're going to do, we're going to cover all those clauses step by step in order to write any

01:38.040 --> 01:39.080
query that you need.

01:39.120 --> 01:41.200
So now we're going to start with two clauses.

01:41.200 --> 01:45.560
That makes the simplest query in SQL the select and from.

01:45.560 --> 01:46.760
So let's start with that.
